stateDiagram-v2
  state "Desktop works" as Working
  state "Broken by update, good entry kept" as BrokenWithGood
  state "Updated again while broken, good entry kept" as BrokenRepeated
  state "Broken, no good entry in boot menu" as BrokenNoGood
  state "Booted from snapshot" as BootedSnapshot
  state "Old version, settings in new format" as OldWithNewSettings
  [*] --> Working
  Working --> Working : update succeeds
  Working --> BrokenWithGood : update breaks the desktop
  Working --> BrokenWithGood : power fails during update
  BrokenWithGood --> BrokenRepeated : update again while broken
  BrokenRepeated --> BrokenRepeated : update again while broken
  BrokenRepeated --> BrokenNoGood : cleanup deletes the old snapshots
  BrokenRepeated --> BrokenNoGood : the ESP fills up and old boot entries go
  BrokenWithGood --> BootedSnapshot : pick the good snapshot in the boot menu
  BrokenRepeated --> BootedSnapshot : pick the good snapshot in the boot menu
  BootedSnapshot --> BrokenWithGood : the picked snapshot was broken too
  BootedSnapshot --> Working : restore and reboot
  BootedSnapshot --> OldWithNewSettings : restore and reboot, but the new version migrated settings
  OldWithNewSettings --> Working : restore the listed home paths
  %% never NoWayBack: Broken, no good entry in boot menu -- When the desktop is broken, the boot menu always still has an entry that worked.
